mh2lm: add gated SweetSpmiInterruptMux with key IRQ consumers (0134)

Add the current XNU's sole SPI 513 callback before GIC EOI and hand it to a
provider-less IOInterruptEventSource on an IOWorkLoop. A static route table
resolves only EE0 IRQ-owned APIDs, maps Power, Volume Down and Volume Up to
consumer callbacks, and handles PMIC-arb v5 channel/peripheral acknowledgement.
The top half masks SPI 513 before EOI; the worker drains/acks and unmasks it,
with bounded failure handling that turns off GIC/PDC/PMIC gates and restores
the existing key poll period. No IOKit or SPMI access occurs in the top half.

Default boot behavior is unchanged. sweetkeysirq=1 tests software workloop
handoff without MMIO gates; =2 arms Power only while retaining 20 ms polling
for the other keys; =3 arms all three keys with a 200 ms recovery poll.
All MMIO gate writes and route configuration are limited to explicit opt-in
modes and verified against the MH2LM owner/APID, PDC and GIC readbacks.

